cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RoboTwin-Plus in your research, please cite this repository as well as the upstream RoboTwin 2.0 and LIBERO-Plus works listed below."
title: "RoboTwin-Plus: Robustness Testing for VLA Policies via Structured Perturbations"
abstract: >-
  RoboTwin-Plus extends the RoboTwin 2.0 bimanual manipulation platform with
  LIBERO-Plus-style structured perturbation categories (objects, background,
  lighting, camera, robot state, language, sensor noise) for systematically
  evaluating the robustness of Vision-Language-Action policies.
authors:
  - name: "RoboTwin-Plus contributors"
type: software
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/markli1hoshipu/Robotwin-plus"
repository-code: "https://github.com/markli1hoshipu/Robotwin-plus"
keywords:
  - robotics
  - manipulation
  - vision-language-action
  - robustness
  - benchmark
  - domain-randomization
references:
  - type: article
    title: "RoboTwin 2.0: A Scalable Data Generator and Benchmark with Strong Domain Randomization for Robust Bimanual Robotic Manipulation"
    authors:
      - name: "Tianxing Chen and the RoboTwin authors"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.18088"
    year: 2025
  - type: article
    title: "LIBERO-Plus"
    authors:
      - name: "LIBERO-Plus authors"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13626"
    year: 2025
